            "agent": "research",
            "ok": true,
            "finding": {
              "summary": "The East depot's inventory policy requires maintaining at least twenty reserve pallets on site to cover supply interruptions. However, the capacity policy limits the East depot to at most twelve reserve pallets to maintain fire-lane clearance. These thresholds conflict because the minimum inventory requirement (20 pallets) exceeds the maximum capacity allowed (12 pallets). The operational risk is that adhering to the inventory policy could violate fire-lane clearance regulations, while following the capacity policy could leave the depot vulnerable to supply interruptions. Approval processes exist for exceptions: reducing reserve stock requires inventory owner's approval, and capacity exceptions require capacity owner's review. The recommendation is to conduct a joint review between inventory and capacity owners to resolve this conflict, as the passages impose incompatible requirements. There is uncertainty due to conflicting thresholds and the need for coordinated decision-making. Conflicting requirements: inventory-policy says \"The East depot must keep at least twenty reserve pallets on site to cover supply interruptions.\"; inventory-policy says \"Reducing reserve stock requires the inventory owner's approval.\"; capacity-policy says \"The East depot may keep at most twelve reserve pallets on site to maintain fire-lane clearance.\"; capacity-policy says \"The capacity owner must review any proposed exception.\" Ask the responsible policy owners to review the conflict together and document a resolution before changing operations. This conclusion is limited to the passages reviewed.",
